## 4. VECTOR III: ZERO-RF LPI/LPD OPTICAL/ACOUSTIC STIGMERGY & QRNG KALMAN-FILTER DIVERGENCE (`INVARIANTS 18 & 24`)

1. **Total RF Silence Under Spectrum Denial (`Invariant 18`):**
   Active radio-frequency (RF) transmitters act as high-contrast beacons for direction-finding SIGINT and radiation-homing munitions. Under `Status(RF_Jamming) = 1` or LPI/LPD (Low Probability of Intercept / Low Probability of Detection) operating modes, swarm nodes disable RF transceivers completely ($\text{Power}_{\text{RF}} = 0\text{ W}$). State commits propagate exclusively via:
   * **Line-of-Sight Ultraviolet (Solar-Blind UV-C) / Near-IR Optical Pulses:** Rapidly attenuated by the atmosphere beyond $100\text{--}300\text{m}$, making signals physically undetectable to standoff SIGINT while providing megabit-per-second peer synchronization within the swarm.
   * **Passive Visual Kinesthetics:** Observing subtle wingtip/attitude micro-oscillations of neighboring nodes via onboard optical cameras.

2. **QRNG Micro-Trajectory Jitter Against Predictive Fire-Control (`Invariant 24`):**
   Automated kinetic interceptors and lead-computing radar trackers rely on Kalman filters ($\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{k|k-1} = \mathbf{F}_k \hat{\mathbf{x}}_{k-1|k-1}$) that assume constant-velocity or constant-turn-rate flight between waypoints. When an autonomous node transits between waypoints where multiple micro-trajectories have equivalent arrival utility ($\Delta U \le \epsilon$), the onboard controller injects continuous hardware Quantum Random Number Generator ($\mathcal{QRNG}_{\text{Hardware}}$) phase jitter into roll/pitch/altitude vectors, forcing external Kalman filter covariance matrices ($\mathbf{P}_{k|k-1}$) to diverge ($\nabla \mathcal{L}_{\text{Tracker}} \to \text{Divergent}$).

