## 5. VECTOR IV: CIVIL AERIAL CURTILAGE DEFENSE, FAA REMOTE-ID HARM BEACONS, & PASSIVE PHOTOGRAMMETRY POISONING (`STIGMERGIC CLASS ASSEMBLY` ISOMORPHISM)

### 5.1 The Mechanistic Mismatch: Warrantless Curtilage Scraping vs. Federal Anti-Jamming Laws
Property owners, farmers, and privacy-conscious operators face systematic low-altitude aerial scraping by insurance underwriting drones (automated roof/property policy cancellation bots), commercial data brokers, and warrantless municipal surveillance fleets. Because shooting or actively jamming an aircraft violates `18 U.S.C. § 32` and `47 U.S.C. § 302a`, corporate operators assume victims are legally defenseless.

### 5.2 The OPSTACK Isomorphism: Passive Curtilage Harm Beacons & Optical-Flow Disruption
1. **FAA Remote-ID (`14 C.F.R. Part 89`) + Acoustic Harm Beacon Emission:**
   Under `14 C.F.R. Part 89`, commercial drones must broadcast unencrypted Wi-Fi/BLE Remote ID packets containing the UAS Serial Number, operator coordinates, and barometric altitude. A repurposed $15 e-waste smartphone (`Invariant 27`) mounted on private property passively ingests Remote ID broadcasts alongside microphone Blade-Pass Frequency (BPF) acoustic Doppler signatures. Whenever a commercial drone drops below navigable airspace into protected residential curtilage (*United States v. Causby*; *Florida v. Jardines*), the local node hashes the packet + acoustic spectrogram (`SHA-256`) and publishes a `SPEC-2026-STIGMERGIC-CLASS-ASSEMBLY-v2.1` **Aerial Trespass Harm Beacon**. Litigation crawler bots aggregate 2,000+ homeowner beacons against the corporate fleet operator, triggering automated mass arbitration or class-action trespass/privacy litigation (`Invariant 11`).
2. **Passive Structure-from-Motion (SfM) Photogrammetry Poisoning (`Invariant 4`):**
   Overhead commercial inspection drones rely on Structure-from-Motion (SfM) and SIFT/ORB feature-matching to stitch 2D frames into 3D property models. By applying 100% lawful, passive architectural surfaces on private roofs and skylights—such as lenticular Moiré interference tiles, retro-reflective phase markers, and angle-dependent chromatic films—each slight change in drone viewing angle $\Delta \theta$ produces a large, non-linear pixel feature shift. The drone's SfM bundle-adjustment solver fails to converge, corrupting unauthorized 3D reconstructions with zero active emissions.

---

## 6. VECTOR V: JURISDICTIONAL BIFURCATION & UNCOOPERATIVE / JUDGMENT-PROOF INTRUSION STATE MACHINE (`INVARIANTS 21, 22, & 30`)

### 6.1 The Mechanistic Mismatch: Judgment-Proof / Dark-Airframe Intrusions vs. Domestic Statutory Exclusivity
Passive `14 C.F.R. Part 89` Remote-ID Harm Beacons (Vector IV) deter financially accountable corporate fleets (underwriters, logistics carriers, data brokers), but fail when an uncooperative, judgment-proof, or hostile airframe disables Remote-ID broadcasts ("dark airframe") and crosses protected perimeter boundaries. Conversely, deploying active RF jammers, protocol-injection exploits, or kinetic counter-UAS interceptors within civil domestic airspace violates federal law (`18 U.S.C. § 32` destruction of aircraft, `18 U.S.C. § 1030` CFAA, `47 U.S.C. § 333` FCC interference prohibition, and `6 U.S.C. § 124n` federal C-UAS exclusivity).

### 6.2 The OPSTACK Isomorphism: Cryptographic `jurisdiction_context` State-Machine Bifurcation (`Invariant 22`)
To handle boundary-crossing adversarial units without violating domestic statutes or export controls (`Invariant 30`), the defense state machine enforces an immutable cryptographic execution gate conditioned on `jurisdiction_context` and `sovereign_defense_token`:

1. **Civil / US Domestic Custody (`jurisdiction_context: "US" | "EU" | "GB"`, `kinetic_or_rf_interdiction_authorized = False`):**
   * **Hard Statutory Lock (`Invariant 21`):** Any state transition requesting active RF jamming, protocol spoofing, or kinetic interdiction evaluates to `commit_state_transition() = False` at the kernel level.
   * **Passive Multi-Lateration (TDoA) Dark-Airframe Tracking:** When an intruding airframe emits zero Remote-ID packets, $N \ge 4$ time-synchronized e-waste edge nodes (`Invariant 27`) compute a passive 3D kinematic track vector $\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{\text{Dark}}(t)$ via acoustic Blade-Pass Frequency (BPF) Time-Difference-of-Arrival ($\Delta \tau_{ij} = (\|\mathbf{x}_{\text{Dark}} - \mathbf{s}_i\| - \|\mathbf{x}_{\text{Dark}} - \mathbf{s}_j\|)/c_{\text{sound}}$) fused with passive optical bearing intersections.
   * **Automated Physical Occlusion & Statutory Interceptor Handoff:** Boundary crossing triggers two 100% lawful domestic state transitions: (a) local physical hardening (actuating physical privacy shutters, canopy occlusion, or asset sheltering within `< 2.0s`), and (b) zero-latency cryptographic emission of the signed 3D TDoA kinematic state vector $\langle \hat{\mathbf{x}}_{\text{Dark}}(t), \hat{\mathbf{v}}_{\text{Dark}}(t), \text{SHA-256}_{\text{Evidence}} \rangle$ to statutorily authorized federal/law-enforcement C-UAS interceptors (`6 U.S.C. § 124n`).

2. **Authorized Conflict Zone / Sovereign Defense Custody (`jurisdiction_context: "CONFLICT_ZONE_AUTHORIZED"`):**
   * **Dual-Key Quorum & LOAC/IHL Gate:** Outside civil domestic jurisdiction, transitioning to active defensive resource allocation requires **both** (a) a valid $N \ge 3f + 1$ BFT Kinematic State-Verification Quorum confirming an uncooperative hostile trajectory violating a sovereign perimeter, and (b) a cryptographically verified `sovereign_defense_authorization_token` attesting compliance with Law of Armed Conflict (LOAC) distinction and proportionality invariants.
   * **Cost-Exchange-Bounded Stigmergic Allocation (`Invariant 30` Abstract Game Theory):** Rather than expending high-cost interceptors on low-cost decoys (negative cost-exchange attrition), authorized defensive nodes execute a decentralized **Marginal Cost-Exchange Gate**:
     $$\text{Allocate}(\text{DefenseNode}_i \to \text{HostileTrack}_k) = 1 \iff C_{\text{Marginal}}(\text{Node}_i) \le \mathbb{E}\left[L_{\text{Asset}}(k)\right] \;\land\; \sum_{j=1}^N \mathbb{I}(\text{Claim}_{j \to k}) < K_k^*$$
     where $C_{\text{Marginal}}(\text{Node}_i)$ is the unit defensive resource cost, $\mathbb{E}[L_{\text{Asset}}(k)]$ is the expected boundary-breach loss of the protected asset, and $K_k^*$ is the Vector I Kademlia XOR redundancy quota. In strict compliance with **22 C.F.R. § 120.34 (ITAR Public Domain)** and **15 C.F.R. § 734.7 (EAR Fundamental Research)**, this layer outputs only an abstract **Target-Assignment & Cost-Exchange State Commit**—never weapon fuzing logic, RF jamming waveforms, or munition guidance firmware.

